                * We'll use the following code from the Unstructured library to demonstrate how tables can be extracted

                !!! note
                    <Your-File-Path> In the below code filename, is the relative path where your PDF is uploaded. To get the correct file path, click on the 'data' folder, select your PDF file, click on [...] and choose Copy Path. Example: filename = "/content/data/CiscoReport.pdf"

                ```py linenums="1"

                import os
                from unstructured.partition.pdf import partition_pdf
                from unstructured.staging.base import elements_to_json

                # Let's load up our PDF and then partition it.
                filename = "<Your-File-Path>"# Use relative path since the file is in the same directory.
                # Extracts the elements from the PDF
                elements = partition_pdf(
                    filename=filename,
                    extract_images_in_pdf=True,
                    strategy="hi_res",
                    infer_table_structure=True,
                    hi_res_model_name="yolox"
                )
                # Let's look at our elements
                elements
                ```

                ![elemebts](./assets/task3/elem.png)

                * Lets grab element 45, as its the one where our table is

                ```py linenums="1"
                elements[45].metadata.text_as_html
                ```

                !!! note
                    If you run the command elements[45].metadata.text_as_html and the output is blank, search through the elements to locate where the first "table" field is defined. Look for the keyword unstructured.documents.elements.Table to identify which row contains your table data. As shown in the above image, the table element is located at unstructured.documents.elements.Table in a specific memory location. In this case, the table appears at row 45, but if the command does not work, manually check the positions where tables are stored. Keep in mind that indexing starts from 0, so row 45 refers to the 46th element in the list.

                <span class="colour" style="color:green">OUTPUT - Example</span>

